(* arith-identity: the fold rules, their guards, and the negative controls
   that show each guard is load-bearing.  Build:  isabelle build -D .

   The session carries THREE theory layers of one denotation, in dependency
   order: ArithIdentity (the shell-int reading `ev`), ArithWidth (the
   machine-width reading the C checked-i64 tier needs, importing
   ArithIdentity), ArithDec (the byte-level decimal rendering the hand-rolled
   itoas need, importing ArithWidth). A failure still names the theory.

   The latter two sat in this directory UNTRACKED and in no ROOT until
   2026-11-09, while C_UB_PROOF.md §14b cited `ArithDec.thy` as the
   mechanization of the decimal renderers — a claim no build reached. They are
   separate SESSIONS only if each gets its own directory; Isabelle rejects two
   sessions sharing one ("Duplicate use of directory"), so they ride in this
   session's `theories` list instead. *)
session ArithIdentity = HOL +
  options [quick_and_dirty = false]
  theories
    ArithIdentity
    ArithWidth
    ArithDec
